    "details": "https://github.com/erlang/otp/security/advisories/GHSA-22cw-4ph4-6447\nreports:\n\n> Erlang/OTP\\'s TLS hostname verification implements a legacy RFC 6125\n> fallback that checks the Subject CommonName when the Subject\n> Alternative Name (SAN) extension is absent, rather than following RFC\n> 9525 which requires validation to fail without SAN. Combined with weak\n> handling of X.509 Name Constraints, this enables man-in-the-middle\n> attacks when an attacker controls a DNS-constrained sub-CA and can\n> intercept network traffic, allowing forgery of certificates for\n> unauthorized domains.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0230",
    "modified": "2026-05-28T00:00:00Z",
    "published": "2026-05-28T00:00:00Z",
